Task: Closing condition demonstration

All four clauses were demonstrated from a copy of the repository taken out of
version control into an empty directory, so nothing in the working tree could
be propping the result up.

1. Core tests from the clean copy: one command, 78 tests, 0 failures, exit 0.

2. The extension installed from that clean copy into the application's own
   configuration directory. The application's log confirms it loaded, and the
   interface was then driven and captured: the File menu opens, a Puncher group
   sits in it, and its submenu carries both commands.

3. The runtime suite run by the real binary from the clean copy: 29 checks, 0
   failures, exit 0.

4. The motion watched twice. Once interactively: the command was run from the
   menu on the bundled sample character, reported eleven produced frames, left
   the original layer alone, and one press of undo removed the whole result -
   the application's own status line said so. Once as frames: every frame of
   the rendered animation was looked at in order, showing the held opening
   beat, one large step, progressively smaller steps as it slows, and the
   landing held at the end.

Found while doing this: the interface driver aimed every click tens of pixels
wide, because it took the window's position inside its frame for its position
on screen. That is why an earlier session concluded synthetic input does not
arrive here and wrote that into the tool documentation as fact. Both the code
and the documentation are corrected, and the corrected driver was used to open
the menu and submenu from coordinates read off a captured image.

